ge>262</fpage>&#x02013;269.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11123301</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib27"><label>27</label><citation citation-type="journal">Opferman, J.T., A. Letai, C. Beard, M.D. Sorcinelli, C.C. Ong, and S.J. Korsmeyer. <year>2003</year>. Development and maintenance of B and T lymphocytes requires antiapoptotic MCL-1. <source>Nature.</source> <volume>426</volume>:<fpage>671</fpage>&#x02013;676.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14668867</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib28"><label>28</label><citation citation-type="journal">Fry, T.J., and C.L. Mackall. <year>2001</year>. Interleukin-7: master regulator of peripheral T-cell homeostasis? <source>Trends Immunol.</source> <volume>22</volume>:<fpage>564</fpage>&#x02013;571.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11574281</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib29"><label>29</label><citation citation-type="journal">Peifer, M., and P. Polakis. <year>2000</year>. Wnt signaling in oncogenesis and embryogenesis&#x02013;a look outside the nucleus. <source>Science.</source> <volume>287</volume>:<fpage>1606</fpage>&#x02013;1609.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10733430</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib30"><label>30</label><citation citation-type="journal">El Kassar, N., P.J. Lucas, D.B. Klug, M. Zamisch, M. Merchant, C.V. Bare, B. Choudhury, S.O. Sharrow, E. Richie, C.L. Mackall, and R.E. Gress. <year>2004</year>. A dose effect of IL-7 on thymocyte development. <source>Blood</source>. <volume>104</volume>:<fpage>1419</fpage>&#x02013;1427.<pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15155461</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>